<p><FONT face="verdana, tahoma" size="2" >Dunno how many of you guys have heard of this "Distributed Computing" thing, but a new project just came out that appears to be very slick and worthwhile.<br>
<br>
"Distributed Computing" is where you take a workload that is too great for a single PC/Server/Cray, split it up into chunks, and have many individual PCs process the data.  This way, with all the PCs we have in the world, you can get MUCH better and faster results than you could running it on a single PC/Server/Cray.<br>
<br>
The new project I'm referring to is <a href="http://members.ud.com/vypc/cancer/" target=_blank>http://members.ud.com/vypc/cancer/</a>.  It's a project which analyzes interactions of drugs with proteins, and the proteins in this case are ones known to be involved with the growth of cancer!<br>
<br>
For the cost of a simple screensaver (FREE), your PC can also help fight cancer.<br>
